    because the leading coefficient ${\boldsymbol{\gamma}}_{1d_{1j}}({\underline{h}})-{\boldsymbol{\gamma}}_{jd_{1j}}({\underline{h}})$ is independent of $h_{r+1}$.

    Second, we let $d_1$ denote the degree of ${\textbf{Q}}_1$ in $z$ and expand
\begin{align}\label{E: second case PET}
