    \end{align*}
    we first show that the family 
    ${\mathcal Q} := \{P_{\underline{\epsilon}}:\; {\underline{\epsilon}}\in\{0,1\}^r\}$ 
    (ordered so that $P_{\underline{1}}$ comes first) descends from ${\mathcal P}=\{P - P(0)\}$. Indeed, ${\mathcal Q}$ is normal, for which it is crucial that $d\geq 2$, since otherwise $P_{\underline{\epsilon}}(z, {\underline{h}}) = \beta_1 z$ for every ${\underline{\epsilon}}$, as the contributions of ${\underline{h}}$ are absorbed into the term not depending on $z$. 
    Moreover, a simple computation gives that
    \begin{align*}
        P_{\underline{\epsilon}}(z,{\underline{h}}) &= \sum_{i=0}^d z^i \sum_{\substack{{\underline{u}}\in{\mathbb N}_0^r:\; |{\underline{u}}|\leq d-i,\\ \mathrm{supp}({\underline{u}})\subseteq\mathrm{supp}({\underline{\epsilon}})}}{{|{\underline{u}}|+i}\choose{{\underline{u}}}}\beta_{|{\underline{u}}|+i} {\underline{h}}^{\underline{u}}, 
    \end{align*}
    and hence the formula \eqref{E: gamma_ji} holds with $w_{{\underline{\epsilon}}{\underline{u}}} = \mathbf{1}(\mathrm{supp}({\underline{u}})\subseteq\mathrm{supp}({\underline{\epsilon}}))$ and $w_{\underline{u}} = 0$. This immediately implies property \eqref{i: w_1} from Definition \ref{D: descendence}. One also sees that for distinct ${\underline{\epsilon}},{\underline{\epsilon}}'\in\{0,1\}^r$, the leading coefficient of 
    $P_{\underline{\epsilon}}-P_{{\underline{\epsilon}}'}$ as a polynomial in $z$ is $d \beta_d ({\underline{\epsilon}}-{\underline{\epsilon}}')\cdot{\underline{h}}$. In particular, the leading coefficient of $P_{\underline{\epsilon}}-P_{{\underline{\epsilon}}'}$ is a multilinear homogeneous polynomial of degree $1$. This gives property \eqref{i: multilinear} of Definition \ref{D: descendence}, and property \eqref{i: leading coeffs} follows since $\beta_d$ is the leading coefficient of $P$. 
    Hence ${\mathcal Q}$ indeed descends from ${\mathcal P}$. This allows us to use Proposition \ref{P: vdC terminates} to find positive integers $r'=O_{d,r}(1)$ and $m_1, \ldots, m_{r'}$ such that ${\mathcal Q}'=\partial_{m_{r'}, \ldots, m_1}{\mathcal Q}$ is linear in $z$ and has size $s:=|{\mathcal Q}'|\ll_{d,r} 1$.

    Since Proposition \ref{P: vdC terminates} also gives that ${\mathcal Q}'$ descends from ${\mathcal P}$, the members of ${\mathcal Q}'$ are multilinear homogeneous polynomials of degree $d-1$ (homogeneity follows from remark \eqref{i: homogeneity} below Definition \ref{D: descendence}). Letting ${\underline{h}} = (h_1, \ldots, h_{r''})$ from now on with  $r'':=r+r'$, we can enumerate the elements of ${\mathcal Q}'$ as
